uiem for Regina chapter of Dark Eras? You should still be able to read it on the Dark Eras Kickstarter page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:07:43-08:00","id":838648,"title":"","content":"I wasn't aware! Thank you<br /> <br /> EDIT: The write-up is interesting but they only get 1 merit which is not really about Covenant secret-powers. Interesting nontheless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 02-28-2016, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:59:02-08:00","id":841453,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind me asking, how does the Gallows Post intend to prevent communication between domains? I mean, having a covenant of messengers makes sense in eras before things like public postal systems became common, but nowadays it seems like the Post couldn't control communications without having an absurdly pervasive and well-organized global conspiracy that literally controls the internet, or seriously wrecking the masquerade by disrupting services to entire metropolitan areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T13:29:14-08:00","id":841474,"title":"","content":"Which is likely why they are a dying Covenant.<br /> <br /> As for powers?<br /> Maybe something like the Animalism power that marks territory, but either blocks the messages/messengers, or just alerts GP legbreakers to come deal with the &quot;Competition&quot;.<br /> Maybe something that lets them manipulate the Cacophony? Vampires seem to get their special take on info from there, so control/manipulation of that might be useful.<br /> Maybe something that lets them embed coded messages into people? Take Joe the traveller, infuse him with the latest Domain gossip/mail, then let him act as a carrier to new Domains.<br /> Or just something that lets them communicate long distances instantly or so. Maybe based on Blood Ties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T13:48:00-08:00","id":841483,"title":"","content":"I could see some variants of the Web and Gilded Cage Disciplines, perhaps with a touch of the Csal\u00e1d's Lithopedia. The latter two offer forms of control over an area or city, while the former involves connections and relationships. I could see them putting all their faith in a bloodline that might have a power that made them relevant. Vampires don't seem like the type to suffer being made redundant well.<br /> <br /> Some might adapt. In one of the Night Horrors book there is a woman with shadow servants who specializes in transporting vampires safely. Information is easy to get across borders, but vampires still might have trouble with it. It seems like a natural evolution of the Gallows Post.<br /> <br /> I wonder if players will be able to be part of the covenant. It would be interesting to be part of a covenant just as it is finding out its irrelevance in the world. It might even make other covenants think twice. Sci-fi and cyberpunk stories have existed for a while and they often don't paint a very optimistic future for the All Night's Society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:50:07-08:00","id":841664,"title":"","content":"You don't actually have to disrupt an entire system to prevent specific groups from using it. Take the internet for example, if you hack the accounts and mailing lists of known Vampires in one city you can then spread your ability to prevent them and those they know from communicating that way. Sure they can stop at a random internet caf\u00e9 and post to Twitter or create anonymous accounts, but unless the receiving party knows where to look it will get lost in the sea of information that is the super highway. Even a phone call requires a number to dial, preventing the sharing of such information, or just eliminating specific paths of communication by polluting it with false communications can go a long way towards isolating individuals who are already limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}